Set the address your devices dial from outside.

This is shared by every way in, which is why it is here rather than
on one of them — and why changing it invalidates every configuration
and link already handed out. It is also the one thing olr cannot work
out for itself: if a name already follows this router's address, use
it — `olr dial show` lists the ones olr keeps current.

Give the host alone. A port here could only be right for one way in;
use --public-port on the one whose forwarded port differs.

Usage:
  olr remote set [flags]
  olr remote set [command]

Available Commands:
  shadowsocks Set the proxy's settings
  wireguard   Set the tunnel's settings

Flags:
      --endpoint string   public name or address your devices dial
  -h, --help              help for set

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")

Use "olr remote set [command] --help" for more information about a command.
